    "title": "Reclaiming What Identity Looks Like with Charlyann Acosta | Q:LV - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Robin Gow ,\n1 days ago On this episode, Robin Gow is joined by Charlyann Acosta, a local artist, community leader, and proud descendent of Taino family. Charlyann explains some of the history of the Taino people, which are one of the largest indigenous groups in the Caribbean, and shares how her queer identity intersects with that culture. Read full article\nRead in NewsBreak 1",
